 2. The concept of a “systems zoo” was invented by Prof. Hartmut Bossel of the
University of Kassel in Germany. His three recent “System Zoo” books contain system
descriptions and simulation-model documentations of more than 100 “animals,”
some of which are included in modifi ed form here. Hartmut Bossel, System Zoo
Simulation Models – Vol. 1: Elementary Systems, Physics, Engineering; Vol. 2: Climate,
Ecosystems, Resources; Vol. 3: Economy, Society, Development. (Norderstedt, Germany:
